From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: Report no disconnection for a refused link

ieee80211_ml_process_link() gives the new link station the flags of the
origin station, WLAN_STA_AUTHORIZED included. Where the link is refused
after that point (the element check of the link, no AID, or the driver
refuses the link station), the failure path frees the link station with
ap_free_sta(). Its ap_sta_set_authorized(0) then reports
AP-STA-DISCONNECTED and the ubus "disassoc" notification with the MLD
address, although the non-AP MLD stays associated over its other links.
A Link Reconfiguration Request that adds a link always reaches this
with an authorized origin station; an association does so only where
the earlier association is still authorized.

Upstream hostap has the same code (main 741d70dd8e32).

Clear the authorized flag of the link station without the event before
it is freed, as ap_free_link_sta() does for the other link stations of
a station that stays associated.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -6676,8 +6676,12 @@ out:
 	if (status != WLAN_STATUS_SUCCESS) {
 		wpa_release_link_auth_ref(origin_sta->wpa_sm,
 					  hapd->mld_link_id, true);
-		if (sta)
+		if (sta) {
+			/* Only this link is refused, so no disconnection is
+			 * reported for the non-AP MLD. */
+			ap_sta_set_authorized_flag(hapd, sta, 0);
 			ap_free_sta(hapd, sta);
+		}
 		return -1;
 	}
 
